# Zerg Grammar
#
# The formal surface grammar of the Zerg language, written in W3C-style EBNF and
# built up one grammar group at a time, from core to minor. This file is the single
# source of truth for what is syntactically well-formed; the prose companion lives in
# docs/grammar.md (and docs/grammar.zh-TW.md).
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notation (W3C-style EBNF)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   name ::= ...     a production; `name` is a non-terminal (lower-kebab-case)
#   'text'           a literal terminal, matched verbatim
#   A B              A followed by B (concatenation)
#   A | B            A or B (alternation)
#   ( A )            grouping
#   A?               zero or one A
#   A*               zero or more A
#   A+               one or more A
#   [a-z]            a character in the given range
#   [^x]             any character except x
#   UPPER-CASE       a lexical token defined under the Lexical group
#   #                a comment, to end of line (same as Zerg's own comment syntax)
#
# ==================================================================================
# 1. nop & program skeleton
# ==================================================================================
# The smallest well-formed Zerg program is a sequence of statements. The first
# statement the grammar defines is `nop` — the placeholder for an empty statement:
# it does nothing and yields nothing, standing in wherever a statement is required
# but none is wanted (an empty function body `fn f() { nop }`, an empty loop
# `for { nop }`). Later groups extend `statement` with the other statement forms.

program   ::= stmt-list
stmt-list ::= stmt-sep* ( statement ( stmt-sep+ statement )* stmt-sep* )?
stmt-sep  ::= NEWLINE | ';'
statement ::= nop                 # extended by later groups: binding, expr-stmt, ...
nop       ::= 'nop'

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lexical tokens referenced above (fully defined in group 2. Lexical)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEWLINE   ::= '\n'                 # a line break terminates a statement
COMMENT   ::= '#' [^\n]*           # to end of line; not a statement

# ==================================================================================
# Roadmap — groups landed one per commit, core to minor
# ==================================================================================
#   2. Lexical        comments, identifiers, keywords, newlines, blocks
#   3. Literals       bool, int (0x/0o/0b), float, rune, byte, str
#   4. Bindings/Expr  ':=', 'mut', operators + precedence
#   5. Functions      'fn' decl, params, defaults, named args, closures, 'return'
#   6. Control flow   'if', 'for ... in', 'match' + patterns
#   7. Types          'struct', 'enum', tuple, 'type X = Y', 'spec'
#   -- minor --       error operators (? ?? ?. ! raise guard); concurrency
#                     (spawn/chan/select/<-); modules (import/pub/package/init);
#                     FFI (extern "C"); defer/del
